DyoSnap: ffmpeg's avfoundation input keeps only one audio frame. While a video frame
is being read, newer audio frames overwrite older ones, so recordings lose about 15%
of their sound and it sounds choppy. This queues audio frames instead.

--- a/libavdevice/avfoundation.m	2026-11-17 17:18:13
+++ b/libavdevice/avfoundation.m	2026-11-17 17:18:13
